BT /F2 13 Tf 35 755 Td (Comprehensive Tomato \(Solanum lycopersicum\) Disease, IPM & Agronomy Guide - Page 1) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 732 Td (1. Fungal & Oomycete Diseases \(Foliar, Fruit & Soil-Borne\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 35 718 Td (A. Early Blight \(Alternaria solani & A. tomatophila\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 706 Td (- Symptoms: Dark brown target-like concentric rings \(bull's-eye lesions\) with yellow halos on older lower leaves; sunken stem cankers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 694 Td (  \(collar rot\) in seedlings; leathery sunken black lesions around the fruit calyx.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 682 Td (- Management: Stake and prune lower leaves \(up to 30 cm\); apply protectant Mancozeb 75 WP \(2.5 g/L\) or Chlorothalonil; rotate systemic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 670 Td (  strobilurins/SDHIs: Azoxystrobin 23 SC \(1 ml/L\), Boscalid, or Difenoconazole \(0.5 ml/L\) to prevent FRAC Group 11 resistance.) Tj ET

BT /F2 9 Tf 35 654 Td (B. Late Blight \(Phytophthora infestans - Oomycete\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 642 Td (- Symptoms: Rapidly expanding, irregular pale-green to dark water-soaked foliar lesions; white downy sporangia on leaf undersides in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 630 Td (  cool, wet weather \(15-22 C, >90% RH\); greasy brown-bronze firm rot on green and ripe fruit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 618 Td (- Management: Forecast via Blightcast models; grow Ph-2/Ph-3 resistant hybrids; prophylactic Mancozeb spray; curative targeted sprays) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 606 Td (  of Cymoxanil + Mancozeb \(2.5 g/L\), Dimethomorph 50 WP \(1 g/L\), Mandipropamid 23.4 SC \(0.8 ml/L\), or Oxathiapiprolin \(FRAC 49\).) Tj ET

BT /F2 9 Tf 35 590 Td (C. Fusarium Wilt \(Fusarium oxysporum f. sp. lycopersici - Races 1, 2, 3\) & Verticillium Wilt \(V. dahliae\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 578 Td (- Symptoms: Unilateral yellowing of lower leaflets \(often on one side of petiole/plant\), progressive upward wilting during midday heat,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 566 Td (  stunted growth, and reddish-brown discoloration of xylem vascular tissue when stem is sliced near soil line.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 554 Td (- Management: Plant I-1, I-2, I-3 \(Fusarium\) and Ve \(Verticillium\) resistant hybrids; graft scions onto resistant interspecific rootstocks) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 542 Td (  \(e.g., S. habrochaites\); maintain soil pH 6.5-7.0 using nitrate-N \(avoid ammonium-N\); drench Trichoderma harzianum \(10 g/L\).) Tj ET

BT /F2 9 Tf 35 526 Td (D. Septoria Leaf Spot \(Septoria lycopersici\), Gray Mold \(Botrytis cinerea\), Powdery Mildew & Southern Blight) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 514 Td (- Septoria: Numerous small \(2-3 mm\) circular spots with gray-white centers, dark margins, and tiny black pycnidia. Spray Copper/Azoxystrobin.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 502 Td (- Gray Mold: Ghost spots \(pale halos\) on fruit and fuzzy gray-brown conidia on pruning wounds in humid greenhouses. Spray Fenhexamid/Fludioxonil.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 490 Td (- Powdery Mildew \(Leveillula taurica / Oidium neolycopersici\): Talc-like white patches or yellow blotches. Spray Wettable Sulfur \(2 g/L\) or Myclobutanil.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 478 Td (- Southern Blight / Collar Rot \(Sclerotium rolfsii\): Rapid wilting with white fan-like mycelial mat and mustard-seed-like brown sclerotia at collar.) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 458 Td (2. Major Bacterial Diseases) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 445 Td (- Bacterial Wilt \(Ralstonia solanacearum\): Sudden green wilting without foliar yellowing; pith browning; milky bacterial ooze streams from cut) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 433 Td (  stem suspended in clear water. Control: Bio-fumigation with brassicas; graft onto Hawaii 7996/eggplant rootstock; drench Pseudomonas fluorescens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 421 Td (- Bacterial Canker \(Clavibacter michiganensis subsp. michiganensis\): 'Firing' \(marginal necrosis\) of leaflets, longitudinal stem cankers, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 409 Td (  diagnostic 'bird's-eye' spots \(dark center with white halo\) on fruit. Control: Hot water seed treatment \(50 C for 25 min\); tool disinfection.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 397 Td (- Bacterial Spot \(Xanthomonas spp.\) & Speck \(Pseudomonas syringae pv. tomato\): Greasy water-soaked leaf spots and raised scabby fruit) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 385 Td (  lesions. Control: Spray Copper Hydroxide + Mancozeb tank-mix \(fixed copper mobilization\), Streptomycin \(where permitted\), or Acibenzolar-S-methyl.) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 365 Td (3. Emerging & High-Impact Viral Diseases & Phytoplasma) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 352 Td (- Tomato Brown Rugose Fruit Virus \(ToBRFV - Tobamovirus\): CRITICAL GLOBAL THREAT. Breaks Tm-2^2 resistance gene. Causes mosaic,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 340 Td (  fern-leaf narrowing, necrotic peduncles, and wrinkled brown 'rugose' blotches on fruit. Spread mechanically by hands, tools, bumblebees, and seed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 328 Td (  Control: Certified GSPP seed; dip tools in 2% Virkon S or 10% trisodium phosphate \(TSP\); deploy newly bred ToBRFV intermediate-resistant hybrids.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 316 Td (- Tomato Yellow Leaf Curl Virus \(TYLCV - Begomovirus\): Vectored by Whitefly \(Bemisia tabaci\). Causes severe stunting, upward cup-like leaf) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 304 Td (  curling, interveinal chlorosis, and flower drop. Control: Grow Ty-1/Ty-2/Ty-3/Ty-6 gene pyramids; 50-mesh insect-proof net houses; vector control.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 292 Td (- Tomato Spotted Wilt Virus \(TSWV - Orthotospovirus\): Vectored by Western Flower Thrips \(Frankliniella occidentalis\). Causes bronzing of upper) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 280 Td (  leaves, tip dieback, and striking concentric yellow/orange ringspots on ripe fruit. Control: Sw-5 resistant cultivars; blue sticky traps; Spinetoram.) Tj ET
