BT /F2 13 Tf 35 755 Td (Comprehensive Tomato \(Solanum lycopersicum\) Disease, IPM & Agronomy Guide - Page 2) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 732 Td (4. Key Insect Pests, Vectors & Root-Knot Nematodes \(IPM & ETL\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 719 Td (- South American Tomato Pinworm \(Tuta absoluta\): Devastating invasive pest. Larvae mine leaf mesophyll creating silvery blotch mines with dark) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 707 Td (  frass, and bore pinholes under fruit calyx. ETL: 1-2 mines/plant or 3-5 moths/pheromone trap/day. Control: Mass trapping \(25-40 water/delta) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 695 Td (  traps/ha\); Nesidiocoris tenuis mirid bug; Trichogramma achaeae; spray Chlorantraniliprole 18.5 SC \(0.3 ml/L\), Spinetoram, or Cyantraniliprole.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 683 Td (- Tomato Fruit Borer \(Helicoverpa armigera\): Larvae bore circular holes into developing fruits with half body outside. ETL: 1 larva/plant or 2%) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 671 Td (  damaged fruit. Control: African Marigold \(Tagetes erecta\) trap crop \(1:16 row ratio\); HaNPV \(250 LE/ha\); Emamectin benzoate or Indoxacarb.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 659 Td (- Whiteflies \(Bemisia tabaci\), Thrips & Aphids: Sap feeders & virus vectors \(TYLCV, TSWV, CMV\). Control: Yellow/Blue sticky traps \(25/ha\);) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 647 Td (  reflective silver plastic mulch; spray Flonicamid 50 WG \(0.3 g/L\), Spiromesifen 22.9 SC \(1 ml/L\), Afidopyropen, or Azadirachtin 10000 ppm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 635 Td (- Two-Spotted Spider Mite \(Tetranychus urticae\) & Russet Mite \(Aculops lycopersici\): Cause bronze stippling, webbing, and russeted cracked stems.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 623 Td (  Control: Release predatory mite Phytoseiulus persimilis; spray Abamectin 1.9 EC \(0.5 ml/L\), Bifenazate, or Fenpyroximate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 611 Td (- Root-Knot Nematodes \(Meloidogyne incognita & M. javanica\): Cause root galls, nutrient starvation, wilting, and predispose roots to Fusarium/Ralstonia.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 599 Td (  Control: Soil solarization; Mi-1.2 resistant varieties \(note: Mi-1 breaks down at soil temps >28 C\); apply Purpureocillium lilacinum or Fluopyram.) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 579 Td (5. Non-Infectious Physiological & Abiotic Disorders) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 566 Td (- Blossom End Rot \(BER\): Sunken, black, leathery necrotic patch at the blossom \(distal\) end of fruit. Caused by localized Calcium \(Ca2+\) deficiency) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 554 Td (  in fruit tissue triggered by erratic soil moisture, high salinity, or excessive Ammonium/Potassium antagonism. Control: Maintain uniform drip moisture;) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 542 Td (  apply Calcium Nitrate \(Ca\(NO3\)2\) via fertigation; foliar spray 0.5% Calcium Chloride or chelated Ca + Boron directly onto young fruit clusters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 530 Td (- Fruit Cracking \(Radial & Concentric\): Caused by rapid water influx after dry spells and wide day/night temp swings. Control: Uniform irrigation + Boron.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 518 Td (- Blotchy Ripening, Yellow Shoulder & Graywall: Green/yellow hard patches on ripe fruit due to Potassium \(K\) deficiency, high fruit temp \(>32 C) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 506 Td (  inhibits lycopene synthesis\), or whitefly feeding. Control: Maintain K:N ratio of 2:1 during fruiting; spray 2% Potassium Sulfate \(0:0:50\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 494 Td (- Catfacing, Puffiness & Sunscald: Catfacing \(puckered scars\) occurs from cold temps \(<13 C\) during flower bud development; Sunscald \(white) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 482 Td (  blistered patches\) results from over-pruning or defoliation. Control: Avoid excessive pruning on sun-exposed sides; apply kaolin clay particle film.) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 462 Td (6. Modern Agronomic Practices, Fertigation & Biosecurity) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 449 Td (- Nursery & Grafting: Raise seedlings in sterilized cocopeat protrays inside 50-mesh insect-proof net houses; splice-graft elite scions onto vigorous) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 437 Td (  solanaceous rootstocks \(Maxifort, Beaufort, or wild brinjal Solanum torvum\) to conquer Bacterial Wilt, Fusarium, Nematodes, and root hypoxia.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 425 Td (- Mulching & Drip Irrigation: Lay 25-30 micron silver-on-black polyethylene mulch on raised beds \(30 cm high\); silver reflects UV light to repel) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 413 Td (  aphids/whiteflies/thrips, while black suppresses weeds and stops soil-to-leaf spore splash of Early/Late Blight and Septoria.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 401 Td (- Precision Fertigation \(Open-Field Hybrid Target: 60-80 t/ha\): Total nutrient budget ~180-200 kg N, 100-120 kg P2O5, 220-250 kg K2O/ha.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 389 Td (  Stage 1 \(Establishment, 1-20 DAT\): High Phosphorus \(19:19:19 + 12:61:0\). Stage 2 \(Vegetative to Flowering, 21-50 DAT\): Balanced NPK + Ca\(NO3\)2) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 377 Td (  + Borax \(prevents flower drop\). Stage 3 \(Fruit Set to Ripening, 51-120+ DAT\): High Potassium \(13:0:45 & 0:0:50\) + MgSO4 for Brix and firmness.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 365 Td (- Standard Genetic Resistance Codes \(Seed Catalog Key\): V \(Verticillium\), F / Fol: 1,2,3 \(Fusarium races\), N \(Nematodes\), T / ToMV \(Tomato) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 353 Td (  Mosaic\), TSWV \(Spotted Wilt\), TYLCV \(Yellow Leaf Curl\), IR: ToBRFV \(Rugose Virus\), Ph / LB \(Late Blight\), AB / EB \(Early Blight\), BW \(Bacterial Wilt\).) Tj ET
